abstract: >-
  OpenGenesis-BioCore is a local-first, extensible bioinformatics platform
  designed for reproducible analysis workflows on Windows and Linux. Version
  0.4.0 retains the canonical small-variant analysis layer introduced in v0.3
  and adds Workflow Engine 2.0 contracts for DAG modeling and planning, typed
  binding, bounded conditional execution, checkpoint/retry/resume planning,
  durable SQLite workflow state and recovery, exact-version reusable workflow
  templates, a browser Workflow Builder, and a persisted Execution Workspace.
  The release retains the C++20 native core, localhost browser interface,
  plugins, pipelines, scientific benchmark gates, and local-first provenance
  model.

